# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the ATH Framework project following the HTML integration guidelines.

## Changes Made

### 1. Added Analytics Script to HTML Files
Modified both source and production HTML files to include the Vercel Web Analytics tracking script:

**Files Modified:**
- `ath-framework/public/index.html` - Source HTML file
- `docs/index.html` - Production HTML file (GitHub Pages deployment)

**Script Added:**
```html
<script>
  window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
```

This script was added in the `<head>` section of both HTML files, just before the closing `</head>` tag, following the Vercel Web Analytics documentation for plain HTML sites.

### 2. Installed Dependencies
- Ran `npm install` in the `ath-framework` directory
- The `@vercel/analytics` package (version ^1.2.2) was already listed in package.json and is now properly installed
- Updated `package-lock.json` to reflect the installed @vercel/analytics package

### 3. Built the Project
- Ran `npm run build` to copy the updated HTML files from `public/` to `docs/` folder
- This ensures the GitHub Pages deployment will have the analytics tracking enabled

## Implementation Details

For this plain HTML project, the analytics implementation follows the HTML-specific guidelines from the Vercel documentation:
- No need to install React/Next.js/Vue components
- No route support (as this is a static HTML site)
- Analytics will start tracking once the site is deployed to Vercel

## How It Works

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. The inline script initializes the `window.va` function queue
2. The deferred script loads from `/_vercel/insights/script.js`
3. Visitors and page views will be automatically tracked
4. Data can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab

## Testing

To verify the implementation:
1. Deploy the site to Vercel
2. Visit the site in a browser
3. Open browser DevTools Network tab
4. Look for a request to `/_vercel/insights/view`
5. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard

## Files Staged for Commit

- `ath-framework/public/index.html` - Added analytics scripts
- `docs/index.html` - Added analytics scripts (production build)
- `ath-framework/package-lock.json` - Updated with @vercel/analytics dependency

## Notes

- The project already had `@vercel/analytics` in package.json, so only installation was needed
- The HTML implementation is the appropriate choice for this static D3.js visualization project
- No route tracking is available with the HTML implementation, which is acceptable for a single-page application
- The implementation preserves all existing code structure and functionality
